## Scope

**In scope**

- Feature or component under test.

**Out of scope**

- What is not tested, and why.

## Strategy

| Level       | What it covers                | Tooling       | Owner  |
| ----------- | ----------------------------- | ------------- | ------ |
| Unit        | Business rules, edge cases    | Test runner   | @owner |
| Integration | Service and database contract | Test runner   | @owner |
| End-to-end  | Critical user journeys        | Browser tests | @owner |
| Performance | Latency and load targets      | Load tool     | @owner |

## Environments

| Environment | Setup                         | Data            | Notes          |
| ----------- | ----------------------------- | --------------- | -------------- |
| Local       | `make test`                   | Fixtures        | Every change   |
| Staging     | `https://staging.example.com` | Anonymized copy | Before release |

## Test cases

| ID    | Scenario           | Expected result             | Priority      | Status                       |
| ----- | ------------------ | --------------------------- | ------------- | ---------------------------- |
| TC-01 | Happy path         | The user completes the task | :priority[P0] | :status[Not run]{color=gray} |
| TC-02 | Invalid input      | A clear error, no data lost | :priority[P1] | :status[Not run]{color=gray} |
| TC-03 | Dependency is down | Graceful fallback           | :priority[P2] | :status[Not run]{color=gray} |

## Entry and exit criteria

::::columns
:::column
**Entry**

- Feature complete and deployed to staging.
- Test data loaded.
:::
:::column
**Exit**

- All P0 and P1 cases pass.
- No open critical or high defects.
:::
::::

## Risks

:::risk{impact=medium likelihood=medium owner=@owner status=open} Risk to coverage or schedule
How we reduce it.
:::

## Schedule

:::timeline
- [ ] **{{today}}** — Test plan approved
- [ ] **YYYY-MM-DD** — Test execution starts
- [ ] **YYYY-MM-DD** — Go/no-go review
:::

:::agent Rules for writing and running tests
- Name automated tests after their case ID (TC-01) so results map back to this plan.
- Update the Status column only from an actual run; never mark a case passed without one.
- Add a case to the table for every new scenario you test.
:::
